y", 91.114, 91.456], ["knelt", 91.456, 91.856], ["the", 92.023, 92.115], ["kingtaker", 92.115, 92.623], ["didn't", 92.623, 93.006], ["he", 93.199, 93.299], ["stepped", 93.299, 93.582], ["in", 93.582, 93.674], ["front", 93.674, 93.874], ["of", 93.874, 93.949], ["me", 93.949, 94.141], ["how", 94.406, 94.498], ["many", 94.498, 94.681], ["crowns", 94.681, 95.106], ["are", 95.106, 95.198], ["in", 95.198, 95.273], ["that", 95.273, 95.439], ["forest", 95.439, 95.939], ["guess", 96.164, 96.531], ["part", 96.71, 97.201], ["is", 97.201, 97.293], ["on", 97.293, 97.385], ["my", 97.385, 97.51], ["profile", 97.51, 98.235]], "lines": [[0.0, 5.271, "In this town, we don't fight wars. Our war beasts do, and the winner keeps the loser's crown."], [5.554, 7.112, "Most beasts carry two or three."], [7.35, 12.003, "The black stag across the river is taller than our church. It carries ninety-nine on its antlers."], [12.269, 16.564, "Lose your crown, and their king owns your town. Today it came for ours."], [16.858, 20.861, "Our war beast is a goat. He ran. So did our army. I didn't."], [21.074, 24.291, "And in front of both towns, their war beast knelt. To me."], [24.459, 30.154, "Their soldiers froze. Their horses knelt too. Then one crown slid off its antlers and landed on my head."], [30.379, 33.925, "Then it laid its neck down like a ramp. You'd climb up, right? So did I."], [34.111, 37.019, "It stood up, and their whole army looked like toy soldiers."], [37.221, 40.034, "Their general yelled, \"The Kingtaker belongs to our king!\""], [40.3, 42.632, "\"Good,\" I said. \"I'll bring him back myself.\""], [42.922, 44.38, "We crossed the river in one step."], [44.606, 48.465, "The king's castle was built out of thrones, one from every town he ever took."], [48.678, 50.661, "But the Kingtaker only won ninety-nine."], [50.928, 54.936, "Then the king walked out, alone. Nobody has ever seen what won him the rest."], [55.197, 59.755, "\"He won me ninety-nine crowns,\" the king said, \"and he never once knelt to me.\""], [60.009, 63.542, "\"A war beast only kneels to its true king. You know what that means.\""], [63.811, 65.363, "I nodded. I had no idea."], [65.647, 67.955, "\"It means those crowns are yours,\" he said."], [68.2, 72.525, "The Kingtaker lowered his head, and all ninety-nine crowns slid down to my feet."], [72.742, 76.785, "That morning, I owned a goat. Now I owned ninety-nine towns."], [77.06, 82.349, "\"In this kingdom, whoever holds the most crowns is king,\" he said. \"And I still hold more than you.\""], [82.671, 85.672, "Then the ground shook. The mountain behind his castle stood up."], [85.863, 90.756, "It was his first war beast. The forest on its head was antlers, and every branch held a crown."], [90.956, 94.141, "His army knelt. The Kingtaker didn't. He stepped in front of me."], [94.406, 96.531, "How many crowns are in that forest? Guess."], [96.71, 98.235, "Part 2 is on my profile."]]}